\details{
For \code{SynSpecies} inputs, the facet chooses among three layout sources:
\itemize{
\item an explicit layout override attached during build
\item a stored \code{\link{SynLayout}} on the \code{SynSpecies} object
\item a newly derived chain layout computed from the annotation and link layers
}

When link panels are present, \code{facet_genomics()} also annotates the final
panel table with source-panel metadata (\code{t_panel}, \code{q_panel}) and vertical
link anchors so that \code{geom_nuclink()} can borrow x ranges from the correct
annotation panels while drawing inside the link panel.
